Description: CVE-2020-7774 - prototype pollution in y18n
 The y18n cache object was created as a plain object literal ({}), which
 inherits from Object.prototype. A crafted locale of "__proto__" combined
 with updateLocale()/__() could pollute Object.prototype. Creating the cache
 with Object.create(null) gives it no prototype, so writes under a
 "__proto__" key stay on the cache object and cannot reach Object.prototype.
 Note: the published npm tarball for y18n@4.0.0 ships only index.js (no test/
 directory), so the upstream test-only hunk is omitted; the security fix is
 fully contained in index.js.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/yargs/y18n/commit/7de58ca0d315990cdb38234e97fc66254cdbcd71
--- a/index.js
+++ b/index.js
@@ -11,7 +11,7 @@ function Y18N (opts) {
   this.fallbackToLanguage = typeof opts.fallbackToLanguage === 'boolean' ? opts.fallbackToLanguage : true

   // internal stuff.
-  this.cache = {}
+  this.cache = Object.create(null)
   this.writeQueue = []
 }
